## 2026-08-28 — Gun pose was killing ALL locomotion (root cause + fix)

**Symptom:** equipping a gun froze the character's legs — walking, running,
jumping and wall-running all stopped animating.

**Root cause: a broken parameter path, not a blending problem.** Wrapping the
locomotion `AnimationNodeStateMachine` in the upper-body `AnimationNodeBlendTree`
moved it from the tree root to a nested node, so its playback path changed from
`parameters/playback` to `parameters/LocoSM/playback`. `EnsurePlayback` still read
the old path, got null, and returned early — which meant `PlayState` could never
`Travel()` the locomotion machine. Locomotion was stuck on whatever it started on,
forever. `UpdateLocoBlend` had the same problem with
`parameters/Locomotion/blend_position`.

Fixed with a `LocoParamPrefix` (`"LocoSM/"` when the upper layer is active, empty
otherwise) applied to both. The bone filter and blend weights were never wrong.

**Worth remembering:** nesting a state machine inside a blend tree silently
re-paths every one of its parameters. Nothing errors — `AnimationTree.Get` on a
bad path just returns null.

**Verification** (`test/TestThirdPerson.tscn`, extended): the harness now drives
the full locomotion set, not just speed — `DebugDriveThirdPerson` takes
`onFloor` / `sliding` / `wallRunning` / `verticalVel` per beat, and the beat list
leads with IDLE, WALKING, RUNNING, JUMPING, FALLING, WALL RUN, SLIDING before the
weapon beats. Captured and read: walking shows a clear mid-stride, jumping shows
knees tucked airborne, wall-run shows stride plus lean — all with the rifle held
in both hands throughout. Legs and arms genuinely combine.

